{
  "abstract": "The reactions e + e \u2212 \u2192 hadrons and e + e + e \u2212 \u2192e + e \u2212 have been studied at the J/gY (3100) resonance). The relative weights of the topological cross sections for fixed charged multiplicity are \u03c3 2 =(32\u00b15)%, \u03c3 4 =(49\u00b18)%, \u03c3 6 =(18\u00b13)%, and \u03c3 8 =(1\u00b10.6)%. The average pion multiplicities are \u3008 n ch \u3009=3.8\u00b10.3 and \u3008n \u03c0 o \u3009=3.1\u00b10.8 . The decay widths are \u0393 e =(4.6\u00b10.8) keV, \u0393 h =(59\u00b124) keV, and \u0393 =(68\u00b126) keV.",
